1
00:00:01,889 --> 00:00:02,679
妈咪 早安
Good morning, mom

2
00:00:02,679 --> 00:00:04,289
早安 小宝贝
Good morning, puppy

3
00:00:04,729 --> 00:00:06,569
今天才周三 对吧 杰
Hump day, am I right, Jay?

4
00:00:06,569 --> 00:00:08,329
你2点半之后就自由了
Your day ends at 2:30

5
00:00:08,329 --> 00:00:10,089
早死早超生
Can't come fast enough.

6
00:00:10,089 --> 00:00:11,219
我指的是退休 杰 你说是不是
Quitting time. Am I right, jay?

7
00:00:11,219 --> 00:00:13,299
我们不要把这点看得过重
Let's not make this a thing.

8
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:16,300
嘿 嘿 嘿 这是啥玩意儿
Whoa, whoa, whoa. What is this?

9
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:18,060
我的水煮蛋呢
Where's my soft-boiled egg?

10
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:19,240
我把它炒了
I scrambled it.

11
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:20,840
尝试一下新鲜事物对你有好处
It's good for you to try new things.

12
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:22,600
我才不要尝试新鲜事物呢
I don't want to try new things.

13
00:00:22,669 --> 00:00:24,319
你不能突然对我这样
You can't just spring this on me.

14
00:00:24,369 --> 00:00:25,469
曼尼 告诉你个坏消息
I have bad news, manny.

15
00:00:25,509 --> 00:00:27,039
生活最刁难你的时候
This is not the biggest curve ball

16
00:00:27,079 --> 00:00:28,769
还没到呢
that life is going to throw you.

17
00:00:28,769 --> 00:00:31,380
哥们儿 不要拒绝新鲜事物
Buddy, don't close yourself off from new things.

18
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:33,650
我有没有跟你说过我对蟹肉饼的心路历程
I ever tell you the story about me and crab cakes?

19
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:35,900
恨之 试之 爱之
Thought I didn't like them, tried them, love them.

20
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,380
那电影版权也能这样吗
Are the movie rights available for that one?

21
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:54,120
邓菲家族春季例赛
Dunphy spring classic.

22
00:00:54,910 --> 00:00:57,370
看下周谁来洗碗
Who's gonna do the dishes for the next week?

23
00:00:57,370 --> 00:00:59,410
男孩大战女孩
Boys versus girls.

24
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:01,060
雄性激素大战雌性激素
Testosterone versus estrogen.

25
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:03,810
站着嘘嘘大战蹲着嘘嘘
Standing up to pee versus the squat.

26
00:01:03,810 --> 00:01:05,510
-菲尔 快开始 -老爸
- Phil, come on! -Dad!

27
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,400
击球失误
Swing and a miss.

28
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:12,900
我摸清了她的路线 卢克
He's in her head, Luke.

29
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:14,940
男孩大获全胜 女生只有流口水的份
And boys rule and girls drool.

30
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:16,680
你才随时流口水
You drool all the time.

31
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:18,220
弄得老妈得带你去看专家
Mom had to take you to a specialist.

32
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:20,060
我还适应我的舌头呢
I'm still growing into my tongue.

33
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:22,240
妈 我能不能和罗宾去看电影
Hey, mom, can I go to the movies with robin?

34
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:25,490
不行 你还在关禁闭
No, you may not, 'cause you are still grounded.

35
00:01:25,490 --> 00:01:27,140
那你能送我回房间吗
Then can I be sent to my room?

36
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:29,100
不行 我们在享受家庭的欢乐时光
No, 'cause we're having some fun family time.

37
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,770
我们整个美丽的下午都呆着外面
We're gonna spend this beautiful afternoon

38
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:33,700
享受新鲜空气 做点运动 好吧
outside in the fresh air, getting some exercise, okay?

39
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:35,740
快投 菲尔
Pitch it, Phil.

40
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:43,440
我勒个去
Oh, well.

41
00:01:43,710 --> 00:01:44,610
游戏结束
That's the game.

42
00:01:44,610 --> 00:01:45,920
什么意思 我们才刚刚开始
What do you mean? We just started.

43
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:46,920
那个是我们唯一的球
That was our only ball.

44
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:48,320
所以呢
So what?

45
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:49,750
游戏就这么结束了 就因为你怕
The game's over just because you're afraid

46
00:01:49,750 --> 00:01:50,950
隔壁的傻蛋克里扎克先生吗
of stupid Mr. Kleezak?

47
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:52,580
对 我才不去他那里
Yep. I'm not going over there.

48
00:01:52,620 --> 00:01:53,340
这比赛真有意思
That was fun.

49
00:01:53,340 --> 00:01:56,860
如果汉尼拔或者弗雷德有孩子
If Hannibal Lecter and Freddy Krueger had a love child,

50
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:58,360
他也会害怕我们的隔壁邻居
he would be afraid of our next-door neighbor.

51
00:01:58,930 --> 00:02:00,930
我通常不对别人做负面评价
I don't have a mean thing to say about anyone,

52
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:03,930
但是克里扎克先生的确
but Mr. Kleezak is...

53
00:02:03,930 --> 00:02:05,900
不是个好人
not a nice person.

54
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:07,180
亲爱的 淡定点
Easy, honey.

55
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:11,000
-海莉 -米奇尔叔叔
- Hey, Haley. - Oh, hey, uncle Mitchell.

56
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:12,640
-你妈在吗 -不在
- Hey, is your mom home? - No.

57
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:14,500
她要带艾丽克斯去看肿瘤医生[谐音口误]
She had to take Alex to the oncologist.

58
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:15,840
天啊 怎么回事
Oh, my god, what's wrong?

59
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:17,240
她要配一副新眼镜
She needed new glasses.

60
00:02:17,610 --> 00:02:20,380
-你是说验光师吧 -随便啦
- Oh. Did you mean optometrist? - Whatever.

61
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:22,460
-要给她带个话吗 -对对
- So, should I give her a message? - Yes, yes.

62
00:02:22,550 --> 00:02:23,950
问她星期六晚上能不能帮忙
Could you ask her if she could possibly babysit

63
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,440
照看一下莉莉
Lily on Saturday night?

64
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,940
我们感激不尽
We'd really, really appreciate it.

65
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:28,380
星期六晚上我们要和
Saturday night, we're having dinner

66
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:30,080
胡焦 朗吉奴斯以及克里斯宾吃饭
with pepper, longinus, and crispin.

67
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:31,580
他们都是同志
They're our gay friends.

68
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:32,860
我觉得大家都知道
I think that was clear.

69
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:35,480
我最近大部分时间都跟
I've been spending a lot of time

70
00:02:35,620 --> 00:02:37,000
异性恋的人呆在一起
with a lot of straight people lately.

71
00:02:37,030 --> 00:02:39,980
亲爱的 我需要跟我的伙计们好好玩一晚
And, darling, I need a night with my homies.

72
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:42,540
-你是说你的同性闺蜜吧 -对
- You mean homos. - Okay. Yeah.

73
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:44,960
或许你留下来照看莉莉会更好
You know what? Maybe you should stay in and babysit.

74
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:46,940
我们的保姆不能来
Yeah, our babysitter bailed,

75
00:02:46,950 --> 00:02:48,620
我们有点小麻烦
and we're kind of in a bind, so --

76
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:49,930
我能行 我能照看莉莉
I can do it. I can watch lily.

77
00:02:49,930 --> 00:02:52,010
我很在行的 我现在就在照看卢克呢
I'm really good. I'm babysitting Luke right now.

78
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:52,920
是吗
Oh, yeah?

79
00:02:53,191 --> 00:02:55,071
你想照看莉莉
You want -- you want to babysit lily?

80
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,640
亲爱的 真的很感谢
Oh, well, that's very sweet, honey,

81
00:02:57,811 --> 00:02:59,871
但是你是个很受欢迎的女孩子
but you're -- you're a very popular girl.

82
00:02:59,871 --> 00:03:01,271
我想你有更好的事情做
I'm sure you have better things to do, so --

83
00:03:01,271 --> 00:03:04,401
真的 我现在很闲
Oh, seriously, I'm totally free.

84
00:03:04,401 --> 00:03:07,501
现代被关禁闭可比古时候糟糕多了
Being grounded is so much worse than it was in the olden days.

85
00:03:07,501 --> 00:03:09,091
我朋友不断给我发短信 更新facebook
My friends text and facebook

86
00:03:09,091 --> 00:03:09,881
谈论他们各种有意思的事情
all the fun stuff they're doing

87
00:03:09,881 --> 00:03:12,571
我却只能呆在家里和老爹玩搭积木
while I'm stuck at home playing jenga with my dad.

88
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:16,120
你说真的吗
Are you serious?

89
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:18,280
你甚至可以不给我钱
You don't even have to pay me.

90
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,960
我发誓把她照顾得妥妥的
I promise I'll take super good care of her.

91
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:22,500
好吧 如此甚好 谢谢了
Okay, well, that would be great. Thank you.

92
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,320
好的 星期六见
Yes, well, we'll see you on Saturday night.

93
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:25,540
-拜拜 亲爱的 -拜
- Bye, sweetie. - Bye.

94
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:27,980
卢克
Luke?

95
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:31,440
卢克
Luke?

96
00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:35,220
你在想些什么
What are you thinking?!

97
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:37,600
海莉是一个甜美时尚的女孩
Haley is a very sweet and fashionable girl,

98
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:39,820
但显然不是一个合格的保姆
but seems hardly a responsible caregiver!

99
00:03:40,140 --> 00:03:41,500
我们需要一名临时看孩子的人
Well, you know what? We needed a sitter.

100
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:42,240
她是我们的家人
She's family.

101
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:43,400
我们就让她试一次吧
I say we give her a shot.

102
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:45,480
试一次 用我们的孩子
A shot? Oh, with our only child?

103
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:46,240
当然 为什么不呢
Sure, why not?

104
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:46,980
如果有什么差错的话
If something goes wrong,

105
00:03:47,041 --> 00:03:49,821
我们只需回到东方 再领养一个
We'll just pop over to the orient and grab another one.

106
00:03:59,240 --> 00:03:59,760
什么
What?

107
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:02,620
我是卢克·邓菲 我住在隔壁
My name is Luke Dunphy. I live next door.

108
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:03,340
你有什么事
What do you want?

109
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:05,240
我想到你的院子里把球拿回来
I want to get our ball from your yard.

110
00:04:06,601 --> 00:04:08,371
我可不想让你把后面搞得一团糟
I don't want you messing around back there.

111
00:04:08,371 --> 00:04:10,161
回家去吧
Just go home.

112
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:11,560
你要去潜水吗
Are you going scuba diving?

113
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:13,340
你为什么要带着个罐子
Why do you have that tank?

114
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:15,681
你聪明吗
You being smart?

115
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,680
你是说在学校吗 还行
You mean in school? Well, I do okay.

116
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:20,660
老师说我容易走神
My teacher says I get distracted.

117
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:22,860
为什么你的鼻子里会有管子
Why do you have that tube in your nose?

118
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:24,160
好玩
For fun.

119
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:26,060
真的吗 我能试试吗
Really? Can I try?

120
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:27,680
这是氧气
It's oxygen.

121
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,280
我们房子里也有
We have that in our house,

122
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:30,520
但我们不需要用罐子装
but we don't need tanks.

123
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:32,780
看在上帝的份上 去拿你的球吧
Oh, for god's sake, just get your ball.

124
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:33,720
好的
Okay.

125
00:04:42,651 --> 00:04:44,021
我的天啊
Oh my god.

126
00:04:44,021 --> 00:04:45,401
我在看新闻
I was watching the news,

127
00:04:45,401 --> 00:04:49,161
又有一群鸟从天空掉下来死了
and another flock of birds fell out of the sky dead.

128
00:04:49,161 --> 00:04:50,291
发生什么事了
What is happening?

129
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:52,020
亲爱的 你不能再看新闻了
Sweetie, you got to stop watching the news.

130
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:56,180
这就是你的解决办法 拥抱无知吗
That's your big solution -- embrace ignorance?

131
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:57,540
你们两个在争辩什么
What are you two arguing about?

132
00:04:57,940 --> 00:04:59,020
算了 我不想知道
Never mind, I don't want to know.

133
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,360
我去去就回
Be back in a couple hours.

134
00:05:01,471 --> 00:05:02,771
你要去哪
Whoa, whoa, whoa, where you going?

135
00:05:02,791 --> 00:05:04,901
去我朋友沃特家看《正午迷情》
To my friend Walt's house to watch "High noon."

136
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:07,560
我喜欢西部电影 越血腥越好
Ooh, I love westerns -- the bloodier, the better.

137
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:08,860
这是我最喜欢的影片类型
that's my favorite type of movie --

138
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,780
这个和任何以啦啦队竞争为背景的电影
That and anything set against the backdrop

139
00:05:10,780 --> 00:05:11,900
都是我的最爱
of competitive cheerleading.

140
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:14,060
沃特是那个总是在玩滑板的那个人吗
Is Walt the one who's always skateboarding?

141
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:16,480
不是 玩那个他的氧气瓶要放哪里
No. Where would he put his oxygen tank?

142
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:18,040
好的 我真迷糊了
Okay, now I'm really confused.

143
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:19,680
你的口气和沃特像极了
You sound like Walt.

144
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:22,080
他也经常犯迷糊 这可真是太搞笑了
He gets confused a lot. It's hilarious.

145
00:05:22,282 --> 00:05:24,552
等等 你说的是克里扎克先生吗
Wait, are we talking about Mr. Kleezak?

146
00:05:24,552 --> 00:05:27,072
是的 我到他的住所去拿回我的球
Yeah. I went over to his house to get my ball,

147
00:05:27,072 --> 00:05:28,942
然后我们就开始一起玩耍了
and we've been hanging out.

148
00:05:28,942 --> 00:05:30,902
你去过克里扎克先生的家吗
You were in Mr. Kleezak's house?

149
00:05:30,902 --> 00:05:32,342
卢克 这可不行
Luke, that is not okay.

150
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:33,160
为什么
Why not?

151
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,240
他人真的很好很有趣
He's really nice and funny.

152
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:36,460
听听这个笑话
Listen to this joke.

153
00:05:36,682 --> 00:05:38,832
好的 两个德国鬼子走进一家酒吧
Okay, two krauts walk into a bar.

154
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:39,620
菲尔 这可不妙
Phil, this is not good.

155
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:40,900
亲爱的 别那么武断
Honey, don't jump to conclusions.

156
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:41,860
让他讲完这个笑话
Let him finish the joke.

157
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,600
有一个是个跛子
And one of them has a limp.

158
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:46,680
你不能再去那个人的家里
You may not go back to that man's house.

159
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:49,180
-为什么 -因为 他是个怪人
- Why not? - Because...he's weird.

160
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:50,860
-而且他不是个好人 -对
- And not very nice. - Yeah.

161
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,660
你们也是这么说我的朋友奥利弗的
That's what you said about my friend Oliver.

162
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:53,220
奥利弗
Oliver.

163
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:55,100
是那个差点把我们车库烧没的人吗
Oliver who almost burned down our garage?

164
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:56,520
他喜欢熔化东西
He likes to melt stuff.

165
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:57,900
说得好像你自己很完美似的
Like you're so perfect.

166
00:05:58,462 --> 00:05:59,962
卢克 对不起 但是你妈妈和我
Luke, I'm sorry, but your mother and I

167
00:05:59,962 --> 00:06:01,302
对此不是很安心
just aren't comfortable with this.

168
00:06:01,302 --> 00:06:02,302
这不公平
That's so unfair.

169
00:06:02,302 --> 00:06:03,332
你们甚至都不了解他
You don't even know him

170
00:06:03,332 --> 00:06:05,402
因为你们害怕跟他说话
'cause you're two afraid to talk to him.

171
00:06:05,402 --> 00:06:06,592
兄弟 我们只是关心你
Buddy, we're just looking out for you.

172
00:06:06,980 --> 00:06:08,720
你们从来都不喜欢我的朋友
You never like any of my friends.

173
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:13,660
我们这么做是对的
We're doing the right thing.

174
00:06:13,980 --> 00:06:14,420
绝对没错
Absolutely.

175
00:06:16,180 --> 00:06:16,880
是吗
Aren't we?

176
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:19,480
我不知道 我是说 他说的有道理
I don't know. I mean, he makes a point.

177
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:20,820
我们不了解那个男人
We don't know the man,

178
00:06:20,820 --> 00:06:23,780
小孩能和老人成为朋友 对吧
and little kids can be friends with old people, right?

179
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:25,280
当然可以 这有很多例子
Of course they can. There's tons of examples.

